entries.def:
κεῖμαι 
[in LXX: Jer.24.1 (יָעַד hoph,), al. ;] 
used as passive of τίθημι (LS, see word), to be laid, to lie; 
__(a) of persons: an infant, Luk.2.12, 16; a dead body, Mat.28.6, Luk.23.53, Jhn.20.12; 
__(b) of things, to lie, be laid or set, stand: Mat.5.14, Jhn.2.6; 19.29; 20.5-7; 21.9, Rev.4.2; 21.16; trop., Θεμέλιος, 1Co.3.11 before prep. with accusative, πρός, Mat.3.10, Luk.3.9; εἰς, Luk.12.19 ἐπί, trop.,…
